flowchart TB
    accTitle: When the background job starts a run
    accDescr: Nextcloud's cron starts the background job of the app every five minutes at most. With scheduled synchronization off, it does nothing. Otherwise it takes the start or the end of the last run that synchronized, a scheduled run or one by hand, whichever is later, and a dry-run only while it is still running. When the interval has passed since then, the job starts a run; otherwise it waits for the next background job.

    cron["Nextcloud's cron starts the job<br>every 5 minutes at most"] --> enabled{"Scheduled<br>synchronization on?"}
    enabled -->|no| off["Nothing to do"]
    enabled -->|yes| last["The start or the end of the last run<br>that synchronized, scheduled or by hand,<br>whichever is later"]
    last --> dryrun["A dry-run counts only<br>while it is still running"]
    dryrun --> passed{"Has the interval<br>passed since then?"}
    passed -->|no| wait["Wait for the next<br>background job"]
    passed -->|yes| run["Start a run"]
    classDef check fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef kept fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef changed fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    class cron,enabled,last,dryrun,passed check
    class off,wait kept
    class run changed
